      "writtenOn": "2023-01-25T15:38:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Strokes use 4 independent floats (-2, 0., stroke radius, style) followed by xRadii and LTRB \u003d\u003e 12 floats.\nHairlines use (-2-xRadii), yRadii, and then LTRB so it\u0027s still 12 floats. We avoid uploading stroke radius of 0 and any style since one is known and style is always mitered in the shader code for hairlines. The (-2-xRadii) lets us use the same test for the first float to determine if the instance is stroked or not, but I suppose in reality this means that proper strokes have a smaller number of attributes than hairlines since its second float is unused.",
